<p>Israeli settlers carried out coordinated overnight attacks from Saturday into Sunday on several Palestinian communities in the occupied West Bank. Reports said homes, buildings and vehicles were set on fire, and Palestinians were beaten or otherwise injured in villages near Jenin and Nablus during Eid al-Fitr. Multiple outlets said the violence spread across several locations, with witnesses describing raids through residential areas as property burned and residents tried to get to safety. The attacks followed the death of 18-year-old Israeli settler Yehuda Sherman, who was reportedly hit by a vehicle driven by a Palestinian while riding a quad bike, the BBC said, providing immediate context for the escalation. Israel&#x27;s army later condemned &quot;violence of any kind,&quot; and reports said Israeli security forces responded, though DW said no arrests were made after the attacks. The episode adds to a broader rise in settler violence in the West Bank since the Gaza war began, and shows how quickly a local incident can drive wider instability across the occupied territory.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/STLEiQQt128vcgL0OJsHZdGwUzGhlC8kOtwt5BEEXd5b_Dn6I84WuYAhdAw33P1SUAHyNlUzv_jIzxmEKacM6SJVWejqaxEzV_85mAddluo6j_921QR6fMrbL-6LBDSTpOq-gFZTBXppbmJ2K68HAu3PseXeijknaVNXk6FBNVSkKIhTL81d8ruYS-w8lEVI_z_qamKaLZ0ocsU2q134J_H3naevwfzKk52vkECTg5EFkLEiNZqjByEYuv6eQGGEpxGmtfoABK2aTe5zf8xA' alt='Image from reporting on settler attacks in the occupied West Bank' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Holiday timing: Al Jazeera reported that the raids struck during Eid al-Fitr, deepening fear for families as dozens of settlers stormed a village near Nablus during a major Muslim holiday.</li><li>Geographic spread: The Guardian said violence hit at least half a dozen locations, including al-Fandaqumiya and Seilat al-Dahr south of Jenin, pointing to a broader pattern rather than a single isolated clash.</li><li>Medical toll: DW reported that Palestinians were hospitalized after the rampage, showing that the damage went beyond arson to direct physical assaults on residents.</li><li>Army response: Al-Monitor said Israel&#x27;s army publicly condemned the attacks afterward, a notable official response even as reports questioned how effective forces were on the ground.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Palestinian residents: Residents told reporters that settlers torched buildings and cars in attacks on several villages, describing direct damage to homes and other civilian property across their communities. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/israeli-settlers-burn-buildings-attacks-west-bank-villages'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li><li>Israeli army: The army condemned &quot;violence of any kind&quot; after the attacks, signaling formal disapproval of the raids. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/israeli-settlers-burn-buildings-attacks-west-bank-villages'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li><li>Witnesses cited by media: Witnesses described coordinated raids in which homes and vehicles were set on fire while security forces stood by. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/22/israeli-settlers-carry-out-series-of-west-bank-attacks-as-security-forces-stand-by'>The Guardian</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/west-bank-israeli-settlers-torch-homes-beat-palestinians/a-76475669'>West Bank: Israeli settlers torch homes, beat Palestinians</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cew719w80g7o'>Israeli settlers target Palestinian villages in occupied West Bank, attacking people and properties</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/israeli-settlers-burn-buildings-attacks-west-bank-villages'>Israeli settlers burn buildings in attacks on West Bank villages</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/3/22/israeli-settlers-violently-storm-through-occupied-west-bank'>Israeli settlers violently s